{% set pageTitle = "AI and user-centred design (UCD)" %}
{% set pageDescription = "This guidance explains how UCD teams can use artificial intelligence (AI) responsibly." %}
{% set pageSection = "AI and user-centred-design" %}
{% set landingPage = true %}
{% set dateUpdated = "September 2026" %}

{% block bodyContent %}

<p>AI is reshaping how we research and design digital services. It gives us new ways to analyse data, prototype, test ideas, learn and streamline workflows.</p>
<p>This guidance applies to UCD teams (including contractors and agency staff) who work on NHS services.</p>
<p>We will continue to evolve and expand it as more teams use AI tools and share what they learn.</p>
<p>This guidance will help your team to:</p>
<ul>
  <li>learn and maintain AI literacy</li>
  <li>be more creative and efficient</li>
  <li>stay ethical, safe and inclusive</li>
  <li>meet UCD standards</li>
</ul>
<p>It does not tell you how to:</p>
<ul>
  <li>choose, design, or use AI tools as part of a service for your end users</li>
  <li>develop production code</li>
  <li>use agentic AI for user research <code>what does this mean?</code></li>
  <li>use AI as a tool for wider design practice, for example for service design or creating design artefacts <code>what do we mean by artifacts?</code></li>
</ul>

